; Moving sprite: queue the sprite after the animation step
;
; Continuation of #R$B9CF after #R$A883. The POP BC takes back the animation counter that #R$A883 has just pushed, so
; that SP is at slot+$12 as the end of #R$B3D8 expects (it adds 4 to reach the next slot). HL points to the frame table
; and E is the frame number: #R$B3D8 takes table[E], adds the column offset in A' and queues the draw command.
;
; A' Column offset of the shifted copy
; E Frame number
; HL Frame table
@label=QueueMovingSprite
c$B9F4 POP BC        ; SP at slot+$12
 $B9F5 JP $B3D8      ; graphics = table[E] + offset; queue it, next slot
